The legal texts come from the Boletim Oficial da República de Cabo Verde (Imprensa Nacional de Cabo Verde), as
published by the Tribunal Constitucional de Cabo Verde (https://www.tribunalconstitucional.cv, "Leis
Constitucionais"):

  Lei Constitucional nº 1/V/99 and the republished Constitution, Suplemento ao Boletim Oficial, I Série, nº 43,
  23 November 1999;
  the rectification of Lei Constitucional nº 1/V/99, Boletim Oficial, I Série, nº 3, 14 February 2000;
  Lei Constitucional nº 1/VII/2010 and the republished Constitution, Boletim Oficial, I Série, nº 17, 3 May 2010;
  retrieved 28 October 2026.

The Código Laboral comes from the Suplemento ao Boletim Oficial, I Série, nº 37, 16 October 2007
(Decreto-Legislativo nº 5/2007), copy held by FAOLEX (FAO), https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/cvi221870original.pdf,
retrieved 30 October 2026.

The Código de Processo Penal comes from the Ministério da Justiça's official edition, Código de Processo Penal de Cabo
Verde (Praia, June 2005), copy held by UNODC SHERLOC,
https://sherloc.unodc.org/cld/uploads/res/document/cdigo-de-processo-penal-de-cabo-verde_html/Cabo_Verde_Code_of_Criminal_Procedure_in_Portuguese.pdf,
retrieved 30 October 2026.

The Código Penal comes from the Ministério da Justiça's official edition, Código Penal de Cabo Verde (Praia, May
2004), copy held by UNODC SHERLOC,
https://sherloc.unodc.org/cld/uploads/res/document/cpv/2003/codigo_penal_html/Codigo_Penal_Cabo_Verde.pdf,
retrieved 30 October 2026.

They are official legislative texts. The Tribunal Constitucional's site states "Todos os direitos reservados" for
the site and no licence for the texts; their copyright status is not confirmed here, and they are reproduced with
the attribution above.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per article, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes, dashes and ligatures were normalised; page headers, page numbers and the gazette's other contents
were left out; part, title, chapter and section headings were gathered in one structure file; and the versions were
arranged as git commits credited to the laws that made each change. The wording of the law was not changed.
Neither the Imprensa Nacional, the Tribunal Constitucional, the Assembleia Nacional, the Ministério da Justiça,
FAO nor UNODC endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
